               kpred:serves       kb:agent-context-dogfooding ;
               kpred:evidence     "HANDOFF.md is 107,738 bytes; HANDOFF-ARCHIVE.md a further 94,002. Every session is instructed to read it first, and what happens instead — in the session that wrote this entry — is a grep for section headers. An unread handoff is not continuity, and the size is the reason it goes unread." ;
               kpred:honest-note  "We hold better raw material than ai-memory does: they reconstruct intent from tool-call observations, while we already have the plan, the statuses and the dependencies as a graph. The missing piece is the compiler and the cap, not the data. Nothing has been built, and the prose handoff should not be deleted before something demonstrably replaces it." ;
               kpred:decision-owner "Matt" .

kb:adopt-capture-allowlist rdf:type ktype:Feature ;
