               kpred:has-status   "speculative" ;
               kpred:seen-in      kb:comp-ai-memory ;
               kpred:description  "ai-memory's allowlist capture mode inverts the default so a repository with no marker file emits no observation at all. Their one-line justification is the whole idea: forgetting a marker then costs recall rather than confidentiality." ;
               kpred:serves       kb:workspace-index ;
               kpred:evidence     "Our workspace sync uses the opposite default: WALK_SKIP_DIRS and WALK_SKIP_FILES in src/lib/stores/workspace.svelte.ts are a hardcoded DENYLIST — everything not named is read. The comment above them records what that cost once already: linking a real workspace imported the task queue, run state, digest, idea list and schedules as six unwanted graphs. A denylist is only ever as complete as the last surprise." ;
               kpred:validates    "src/lib/rdf/retention.ts already fails in the safe direction on a different axis — an unclassified predicate defaults to judgment and is therefore protected from archiving. Same reasoning: when the default will sometimes be wrong, be wrong in the direction that costs convenience rather than the direction that costs the user something they cannot get back." ;
               kpred:honest-note  "An inverted default is a breaking change to how linking a folder behaves, so this is a decision about user experience, not only about safety." ;
               kpred:decision-owner "Matt" .

