kb:adopt-divergence-merge rdf:type ktype:Feature ;
               rdfs:label   "Divergent-graph merge that preserves both sides until resolved" ;
               kpred:part-of      kb:competitive-landscape ;
               kpred:has-status   "speculative" ;
               kpred:seen-in      kb:comp-megamemory ;
               kpred:description  "When two copies of a graph diverge, group the conflicting entities under one merge id and keep BOTH as labelled variants until a human resolves them — never silently pick a side, and never lose the loser. MegaMemory resolves by re-reading the current source and writing what the code actually reflects, carrying a verification reason alongside the resolution rather than a bare choice." ;
               kpred:serves       kb:wf-review ;
               kpred:serves       kb:dichotomy ;
               kpred:honest-note  "We already hold the harder half — semantic-diff, merge-aliases, merge-band, and a review tab with merge proposals — and TTL merges textually, so we never needed their merge CLI at all. What is worth taking is narrower than the machinery: the labelled-variant HOLDING PATTERN, so that an unresolved divergence is a visible state rather than a decision forced at merge time." ;
               kpred:open-question "Whether our existing merge path records the evidence behind a resolution or only its outcome was NOT established when this entry was written. Check before claiming a gap." .

