kb:ref-diffusers rdf:type      ktype:Reference ;
               rdfs:label   "huggingface/diffusers — the image-model library" ;
               kpred:part-of      kb:competitive-landscape ;
               hnav:order   24 ;
               kpred:repo-url     "https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers" ;
               kpred:license      "Apache-2.0" ;
               kpred:copy-permitted "yes — Apache-2.0 for the CODE. The WEIGHTS are licensed separately." ;
               kpred:stars        34401 ;
               kpred:last-push    "2026-08-28"^^xsd:date ;
               kpred:description  "The standard Python library for diffusion models. Apache-2.0 and actively maintained, so the harness is unambiguously usable; what it loads is a separate question." ;
               kpred:honest-note  "CODE LICENCE IS NOT WEIGHT LICENCE, and this is the distinction that matters for 'open weight if possible'. Stability-AI/generative-models is MIT for the code while the Stable Diffusion weights ship under CreativeML OpenRAIL-M / OpenRAIL++ — open to download and run, with BEHAVIOURAL USE RESTRICTIONS attached, which is not OSI-open. That is acceptable for a local personal tool and is a real constraint on anything we redistribute or host. Check the weight card, never the repo badge." ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:meme-with-context ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:asset-generation .

kb:ref-comfyui rdf:type        ktype:Reference ;
               rdfs:label   "ComfyUI — a local generation runtime (GPL-3.0)" ;
               kpred:part-of      kb:competitive-landscape ;
               hnav:order   25 ;
               kpred:repo-url     "https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI" ;
               kpred:license      "GPL-3.0" ;
               kpred:copy-permitted "as a SEPARATE PROCESS over HTTP, yes. Bundling or linking would raise GPL obligations on what links it." ;
               kpred:stars        130450 ;
               kpred:last-push    "2026-08-28"^^xsd:date ;
               kpred:description  "The de-facto local diffusion runtime, 130k stars and pushed daily. Node-graph workflows map unusually well onto this product's own shape: a ComfyUI workflow IS a graph, and one could plausibly be generated from ours." ;
               kpred:honest-note  "GPL-3.0 IS THE ONLY LICENCE IN THIS SET THAT CONSTRAINS US, and the constraint is manageable rather than fatal: run it as the user's own sidecar over HTTP — which is what the Integration Boundaries rule requires of any 'backend' anyway — and it stays arm's length. Do not vendor it, and do not let a Reckons.AI process link it. This is a reading, not legal advice." ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:meme-with-context ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:asset-generation .

kb:ref-liveportrait rdf:type   ktype:Reference ;
               rdfs:label   "LivePortrait — expression transfer, REFUSED by the licence gate" ;
               kpred:part-of      kb:competitive-landscape ;
               hnav:order   26 ;
               kpred:repo-url     "https://github.com/KlingAIResearch/LivePortrait" ;
               kpred:license      "NOASSERTION" ;
               kpred:copy-permitted "NO — GitHub reports no recognised licence. Not usable until that changes." ;
               kpred:stars        18979 ;
               kpred:last-push    "2026-06-01"^^xsd:date ;
               kpred:description  "Drives a still portrait with a driving video, which is exactly 'the character in the meme, with the reaction defined' from F161. Technically the closest thing to the hard part of that story." ;
               kpred:honest-note  "AND IT IS THE ONE WE CANNOT USE. The API reports NOASSERTION — no licence GitHub recognises — so the deterministic gate that cleared every other repo in this graph fails this one. Recorded rather than quietly dropped, because the capability is the right shape and someone will find it again: if it is ever relicensed, revisit. The repo has also moved owner (KwaiVGI to KlingAIResearch), which is its own signal about stability." ;
               kpred:relates-to   kb:meme-with-context .
